            </h3>
            <h4>Since AD only captures the lastLogonTimestamp when the domain controller is locally logged on by the user, the value will be set to 0 for all other logons.   To work around this you can follow the below steps to create a <i>Scheduled Search</i> to update the <i>lastLogon</i> and <i>lastLogonTimestamp</i> values in the $tok_usr_lkp$ to use Windows Successful Logon Events to update these field in the $tok_user_lkp$.
